libtheora 1.2.0 encoder: shifts with undefined behaviour (UBSan, fuse_ui_theora_video under the fuse-asan preset).
Left shifts of negative signed values become multiplications by the same power of two, and the 64-bit token flag
masks shift an unsigned 1 (bit 63 of a signed 1<<63 does not fit). Every result is the same value as before on the
two's-complement targets FUSE builds for; only the undefined behaviour goes.
  lib/analyze.c   oc_mb_activity: edge-energy sums of pixel differences (x<<1 -> x*2)
  lib/enquant.c   oc_enc_quantize_c: val<<1 -> val*2
  lib/fdct.c      oc_enc_fdct8x8_c: _x[i]<<2 -> _x[i]*4
  lib/mcenc.c     full-pel -> half-pel motion vectors (v<<1 -> v*2)
  lib/tokenize.c  oc_analyze_token / zero-run flags: (ogg_int64_t)1<<zzi -> unsigned shift, then the signed type

